see-through-hash-reader.patch  Opus team 5, NL-010 roadmap step 5 (5.5 the deep link in, 5.6 the sky re-lifted, 5.8 the way home)
Licence: CERN-OHL-S v2, as see-through/202610050609/ (LICENSE.md:3-6). For a LATER See Through dated folder: See Through is
untouchable in Edition 5, so nothing here is applied to the repository by Opus team 5.
Base: kuiper-belt@96736f55c2137defcf02c898f8f2b0d04374d74b see-through/202610050609/ (descent.js, kuiper-law.js).
Apply, from the kuiper-belt root, with <stamp> the new folder's UTC minute:
    cp -r see-through/202610050609 see-through/<stamp>
    (cd see-through/<stamp> && patch -p1 < ../../editions/202611012135/handoff/05-see-through/see-through-hash-reader.patch)
    then move the pointer see-through/index.html in its three places (:7, :11, :12) to <stamp>/ and add the README entry.
What it adds (descent.js; the 13 controls, flyTo, flightDepth, the layout and the refusal words are unchanged):
  #repo=<name>      lights the stars whose keys fall in that repository's ranges (cosmos/wafer.tsv walked as the engine
                    does); note "<REPO> · n OF <NP> STARS"; unknown: "NO REPOSITORY CALLED <NAME>"
  #key=<k>[&space=<s>]  identity: the star that lands on substation j (box pre-filled, "THE STAR THAT LANDS ON <NAME>.
                    PRESS GO"), else one amber ring at KuiperLaw.place(k), "KEY <k> · A LINE OF CODE, NOT A SUBSTATION";
                    k >= SPACE: "KEY <k> IS BEYOND THIS SKY"; space differing from SPACE remaps a star key by its formula,
                    "STAR KEY REMAPPED · SKY <s> → <SPACE> · …"
  #sub=<name>       the box and GO, exactly as typed (existing words "NO SUBSTATION NAME HERE CONTAINS THAT. TRY ANOTHER NAME")
  #view=kuiper|map|sat|3d   after the flight; other fields: "LINK FIELD <NAME> NOT UNDERSTOOD"
  on arrival:       history.replaceState '#key=<subKey>&space=<SPACE>&sub=<name>'; __descent.link() returns it
  the way home:     X at the stars stage (nothing to undo) -> history.back() for a same-origin referrer, else ../../editions/;
                    aria-label "back to the Kuiper" there; the card's 44 px row "STAR KEY <k> · OPEN IT ON THE KUIPER" ->
                    ../../editions/#key=<k>; the credit line "Stars placed by the Kuiper law (kuiper-belt@96736f5, SPACE …)"
  sky:              kuiper-law.js SPACE 63,340,120,796 (cosmos/wafer-meta.json:4 at 96736f5); descent.js reads
                    ../../cosmos/wafer-meta.json and __descent.sky() says {space, spaceSource: 'wafer-meta' | 'frozen …'}
Measured on a scratch site (lead, Pixel 7, SwiftShader): see handoff/05-see-through/EVIDENCE.md "The See Through patch".

